From a2e59249c17018b86e22d559857804684af26bbb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Iaroslav Voitovych <yaroslav.voytovych@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 06:48:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Bluetooth: btusb: Drop deferred URBs under txlock on a
 failed resume

When btusb_resume() cannot submit the interrupt or bulk URB, it drops
the deferred URBs without txlock and only then clears BTUSB_SUSPENDING
under it. A sender that takes txlock in between still sees the flag
and anchors its URB on data->deferred. That is after the only point
where this resume drops deferred URBs, so the URB stays deferred until
the next suspend and resume, and an HCI command in it times out.

Do both under txlock, so that a sender either anchors its URB before
the drop, and the URB is dropped with the others, or sees the flag
cleared and submits it. This relies on the sender anchoring under
txlock, which the previous patch makes it do. btusb_resume() already
takes the anchor's lock inside txlock, so the lock order does not
change, and btusb_discard_deferred() may run with interrupts disabled.

The two failure branches now share the label that ends a resume with
HCI closed, and drop the deferred URBs only when an error was returned.

Fixes: 7bee549e197c ("Bluetooth: Add USB autosuspend support to btusb driver")
---
Tested in QEMU with a debug-only delay in the failure path and a second
command sent inside it: the deferred anchor was left non-empty after
the failed resume without this patch (3 of 3 runs) and was empty with
it (3 of 3).

 drivers/bluetooth/btusb_main.c | 12 ++++++++----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/btusb_main.c b/drivers/bluetooth/btusb_main.c
index e18b124d0bb7..3861669460d5 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/btusb_main.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/btusb_main.c
@@ -5061,7 +5061,7 @@ static int btusb_resume(struct usb_interface *intf)
 		err = btusb_submit_intr_urb(hdev, GFP_NOIO);
 		if (err < 0) {
 			clear_bit(BTUSB_INTR_RUNNING, &data->flags);
-			goto failed;
+			goto done;
 		}
 	}
 
@@ -5069,7 +5069,7 @@ static int btusb_resume(struct usb_interface *intf)
 		err = btusb_submit_bulk_urb(hdev, GFP_NOIO);
 		if (err < 0) {
 			clear_bit(BTUSB_BULK_RUNNING, &data->flags);
-			goto failed;
+			goto done;
 		}
 
 		btusb_submit_bulk_urb(hdev, GFP_NOIO);
@@ -5093,10 +5093,14 @@ static int btusb_resume(struct usb_interface *intf)
 
 	return 0;
 
-failed:
-	btusb_discard_deferred(data);
 done:
 	spin_lock_irq(&data->txlock);
+	/* Drop the deferred URBs and clear BTUSB_SUSPENDING in one critical
+	 * section: a sender that anchored a URB after the drop but before
+	 * the flag was cleared would leave it parked until the next resume.
+	 */
+	if (err)
+		btusb_discard_deferred(data);
 	clear_bit(BTUSB_SUSPENDING, &data->flags);
 	spin_unlock_irq(&data->txlock);
 
